{"name":"Winter Storm","hex":"#4b7079","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winter storm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A meteorological event in which the dominant varieties of precipitation are forms that only occur at cold temperatures, such as snow or sleet, or a rainstorm in which ground temperatures are cold enough to allow ice to form."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winter_storm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winter storm watch","blocks":[{"text":"A winter storm watch is a warning in the United States issued by the National Weather Service when there is a possibility of heavy snow or potential of significant ice accumulations at least 24 hours before a storm that has a risk of being hazardous."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_storm_watch","wikidata":"Q15222821"},{"title":"Winter storm warning","blocks":[{"text":"A winter storm warning is a hazardous weather statement issued by Weather Forecast Offices (WFO) of the National Weather Service (NWS) in the United States to alert the public that a winter storm is occurring or is about to occur in the area, usually within 36 hours of the storm's onset."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Yearly_avg_Winter_Storm_Warnings_CONUS.png/330px-Yearly_avg_Winter_Storm_Warnings_CONUS.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_storm_warning","wikidata":"Q8026410"},{"title":"Winter storm","blocks":[{"text":"A winter storm is an event in which wind coincides with varieties of precipitation that only occur at freezing temperatures, such as snow, mixed snow and rain, or freezing rain. In temperate continental and subarctic climates, these storms are not necessarily restricted to the winter season, but may occur in the late autumn and early spring as well. A snowstorm with strong winds and low visibility is called a blizzard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Winter_Storm_Jonas_2016_NYC_Pershing_Square.jpg/330px-Winter_Storm_Jonas_2016_NYC_Pershing_Square.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_storm","wikidata":"Q75079023"},{"title":"Winter","blocks":[{"text":"Winter is the coldest and darkest season of the year in temperate and polar climates. It occurs after autumn and before spring, when the hemisphere is oriented away from the Sun as a result of the tilt of Earth's axis. Different cultures define different dates as the start of winter, and some use a definition based on weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/330px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter","wikidata":"Q1311"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/West_Virginia_National_Guard_members_conduct_road_clearing_and_debris_removal_operations.jpg/500px-West_Virginia_National_Guard_members_conduct_road_clearing_and_debris_removal_operations.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/West_Virginia_National_Guard_members_conduct_road_clearing_and_debris_removal_operations.jpg/1280px-West_Virginia_National_Guard_members_conduct_road_clearing_and_debris_removal_operations.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/West_Virginia_National_Guard_members_conduct_road_clearing_and_debris_removal_operations.jpg/500px-West_Virginia_National_Guard_members_conduct_road_clearing_and_debris_removal_operations.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"National Guard members clear a road of fallen trees after a February 2021 winter storm in Putnam